## Latest Dallas Cowboys game (based on sources found)

**When & where:** **Friday, Aug. 28, 2026** — **AT&T Stadium, Arlington, Texas**. (NFL.com lists this as the Cowboys’ “PREVIOUS GAME”; Saints recap and ESPN recap also place it at AT&T Stadium in Arlington.)  
Sources: NFL.com team page; NewOrleansSaints.com recap; ESPN recap.

**Opponent:** **New Orleans Saints**  
Sources: NFL.com; NewOrleansSaints.com; ESPN.

**Result:** **Saints 27, Cowboys 24** (preseason). The Saints won on a **53-yard field goal by Daniel Carlson with 1:55 left**.  
Sources: NewOrleansSaints.com recap; ESPN recap.

**How the game went (high level):**
- ESPN reports **Sam Howell threw two 4th-quarter TD passes and had a tying 2-point conversion run** as Dallas **erased a 15-point deficit**, but New Orleans ultimately won late on Carlson’s kick.  
- ESPN also notes **Brandon Aubrey** made field goals of **49, 51, and 58 yards** (and missed from 57).  
Sources: ESPN recap; NewOrleansSaints.com recap.

**Weather in the city (Arlington) during the game:** The NFLWeather listing for **08/28/26 08:00 PM EDT** (Saints at Cowboys) shows **94°F and “Clear”**, with **east wind 6 mph** (it also notes the stadium as a dome/retractable-roof type entry, while still showing outside conditions).  
Source: NFLWeather.com team page for the Cowboys.

